From a5338cd0cde7c96947332fc7da15df63dcd5a208 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Baron <dbaron@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 10:01:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [Backport] CVE-2026-119269 and CVE-2026-76031 (2/2)

Manual cherry-pick of patch originally reviewed on
https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8641583:
Correct cross-origin check for relatedTarget to handle null execution context.

This fixes the cross-origin check for relatedTarget for both of the
fixes in commit bb79a99bd4473e26031cd5433e34d047fa527f3c to handle null
execution context better (by treating it as cross-origin).

This also changes the defense-in-depth part of the fix to CHECK() rather
than setting relatedTarget to null, since I think that's more
appropriate for a defense-in-depth check (and if we're actually
hitting it we may need to fix the callers that are causing it in other
ways).

Fixed: 577072000
Bug: 572556403, 574379564, 574843953, 577359831
Change-Id: I954eadb02e7a9bec59c0a0306d62cbdfad3543ea
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8641583
